.SH NAME
abacus-scan - Run scanners and ingest results into the graph


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBabacus scan [type] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs all configured scanners (or a specific one by ID) and ingests discovered nodes and edges into the graph database.

.PP
Scanners run in two phases: scan-phase discovers nodes, then link-phase resolves
cross-references between them. Results are upserted so repeated scans are safe.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for scan


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--db\fP=".abacus/abacus.db"
	Path to the database file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output in JSON format

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Enable verbose output


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  $ abacus scan
  $ abacus scan express
  $ abacus scan prisma --json
  $ abacus scan --verbose
.EE


